                    # 2. The occurrence spans the left s_{m-1} and the middle character, but this is not possible unless x is of length 1 and the first character of s_{m-1} matches
                    # So the only possibility is that x is entirely within the left s_{m-1} and starts at its first position
                    # So the count is the same as count_start(m-1, x)
                    return count_start(m-1, x)

                # Now, for each split l, we need to find the number of times prefix appears at the end of s_{k-1} and suffix at the start of s_{k-1}
                # The cross term is the product of these two counts
